<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS1.p1.10" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k^{\epsilon}_{1}(y,x)=e^{-\frac{\|y-x\|^{2}}{\epsilon}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>k</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>ϵ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>ϵ</mi></mfrac></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k^{\epsilon}_{1}(y,x)=e^{-\frac{\|y-x\|^{2}}{\epsilon}}</annotation></semantics></math>. This loss involves only a single learnable map <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi_{0\to 1}^{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>ψ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi_{0\to 1}^{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>, and therefore can be used to directly train <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi_{0\to 1}^{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>ψ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi_{0\to 1}^{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>. During training, the expectations in <a href="#S3.E13" title="Equation 13 ‣ 3.1 First-Order Approximation ‣ 3 Long-Short Flow-Map Perspective ‣ A Long-Short Flow-Map Perspective for Drifting Models" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Equation 13</span></a> are estimated by Monte Carlo using samples within each mini-batch. Once learned, it naturally yields a one-step generator by sampling <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{0}\sim p_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{0}\sim p_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> and computing <math id="S3.SS1.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi_{0\to 1}^{\theta}(x_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>ψ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi_{0\to 1}^{\theta}(x_{0})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">In this loss, the residual term <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}(\theta)\triangleq\frac{\mathbb{E}_{x_{1}\sim p_{1}}\!\big[(x_{1}-\psi^{\theta}_{0\to 1}(x_{0}))\,k^{\epsilon}_{1}(x_{1},\psi^{\theta}_{0\to 1}(x_{0}))\big]}{\mathbb{E}_{x_{1}\sim p_{1}}\!\big[k^{\epsilon}_{1}(x_{1},\psi^{\theta}_{0\to 1}(x_{0}))\big]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≜</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.710em" minsize="1.710em">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ψ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>k</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>ϵ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ψ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.710em" minsize="1.710em">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.710em" minsize="1.710em">[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>k</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>ϵ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ψ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.710em" minsize="1.710em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}(\theta)\triangleq\frac{\mathbb{E}_{x_{1}\sim p_{1}}\!\big[(x_{1}-\psi^{\theta}_{0\to 1}(x_{0}))\,k^{\epsilon}_{1}(x_{1},\psi^{\theta}_{0\to 1}(x_{0}))\big]}{\mathbb{E}_{x_{1}\sim p_{1}}\!\big[k^{\epsilon}_{1}(x_{1},\psi^{\theta}_{0\to 1}(x_{0}))\big]}</annotation></semantics></math>is induced by the closed-form solution associated with an infinitesimally short terminal map <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi^{\theta}_{1-\Delta t\to 1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>ψ</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi^{\theta}_{1-\Delta t\to 1}</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta t\to 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta t\to 0</annotation></semantics></math>, and it serves as an effective supervisory signal for learning the long map <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi^{\theta}_{0\to 1-\Delta t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>ψ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi^{\theta}_{0\to 1-\Delta t}</annotation></semantics></math>. According to our derivation, when <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi^{\theta}_{0\to 1}(x_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>ψ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi^{\theta}_{0\to 1}(x_{0})</annotation></semantics></math> matches the desired transport, the model output and the <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{sg}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>sg</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{sg}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math> target coincide, and <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math> attains its optimum. Moreover, <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{R}(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{R}(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math> admits a concrete interpretation: it is a regression-optimal, kernel-weighted conditional expectation that quantifies the discrepancy between the generated point <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi^{\theta}_{0\to 1}(x_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>ψ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi^{\theta}_{0\to 1}(x_{0})</annotation></semantics></math> and the target distribution <math id="S3.SS1.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, and the loss minimizes this discrepancy in the least-squares sense.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.2 </span>Second-Order Approximation</h3>

<figure id="S3.SS2.fig1" class="ltx_figure ltx_align_floatright" style="width:50%;"><img src="2602.20463v1/drifting_first2_4.png" id="S3.SS2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:238/134;" width="238" height="134" alt="[Uncaptioned image]">
</figure>
<div id="S3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">In the discussion above, we approximated the short flow map using a first-order forward Euler method and then applied the closed-form solution. To obtain a more accurate estimation, here we instead use a second-order trapezoidal rule to approximate the evolution over <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[1-\Delta t,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[1-\Delta t,1]</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
<table id="S3.E14" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="S3.E14X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E14X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\psi^{\theta}_{0\to 1}(x_{0})\approx\psi^{\theta}_{0\to 1-\Delta t}(x_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>ψ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ψ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\psi^{\theta}_{0\to 1}(x_{0})\approx\psi^{\theta}_{0\to 1-\Delta t}(x_{0})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E14X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+\frac{\Delta t}{2}(u_{1-\Delta t}(\psi^{\theta}_{0\to 1-\Delta t}(x_{0}))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ψ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\frac{\Delta t}{2}(u_{1-\Delta t}(\psi^{\theta}_{0\to 1-\Delta t}(x_{0}))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(14)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S3.E14Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E14Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+u_{1^{-}}(\psi^{\theta}_{0\to 1}(x_{0})))." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo fence="true" rspace="0em">OPEN</mo><mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><msup><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ψ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+u_{1^{-}}(\psi^{\theta}_{0\to 1}(x_{0}))).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">As in <a href="#S3.E12" title="Equation 12 ‣ 3.1 First-Order Approximation ‣ 3 Long-Short Flow-Map Perspective ‣ A Long-Short Flow-Map Perspective for Drifting Models" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Equation 12</span></a>, we use the Flow Matching closed-form solution for the velocity on the interval <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[1-\Delta t,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[1-\Delta t,1]</annotation></semantics></math>. The main technical issue is that we require a closed-form expression for the endpoint velocity <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{1^{-}}=\lim_{t\to 1^{-}}u_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><msup><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo></msup></msub><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.167em">lim</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo></msup></mrow></msub><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{1^{-}}=\lim_{t\to 1^{-}}u_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>, which is given by the following theorem.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 3.1</span></span><span id="S3.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Closed-Form Solution of the Endpoint Velocity)<span id="S3.Thmtheorem1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S3.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.Thmtheorem1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For Flow Matching, under mild smoothness assumptions on the underlying distributions, the optimal velocity satisfies <math id="S3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lim_{t\to 1^{-}}u_{t}^{*}(x)=x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>lim</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mrow><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lim_{t\to 1^{-}}u_{t}^{*}(x)=x</annotation></semantics></math>. Consequently, the left-limit endpoint velocity <math id="S3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{1^{-}}^{*}(x)\triangleq\lim_{t\to 1^{-}}u_{t}^{*}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>u</mi><msup><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo></msup><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">≜</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0.1389em" rspace="0.167em">lim</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mrow><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{1^{-}}^{*}(x)\triangleq\lim_{t\to 1^{-}}u_{t}^{*}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> admits the closed form for any <math id="S3.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t\in[0,1)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t\in[0,1)</annotation></semantics></math></span></p>
<table id="S3.E15" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="S3.E15X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E15X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle u^{*}_{1^{-}}(x)=\mathbb{E}_{x_{t}\sim p_{t|1}(x_{t}|x)}[\frac{x-x_{t}}{1-t}]=\frac{\mathbb{E}_{x_{t}\sim p_{t}}[\frac{x-x_{t}}{1-t}k_{t}(x,x_{t})]}{\mathbb{E}_{x_{t}\sim p_{t}}[k_{t}(x,x_{t})]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>u</mi><msup><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo></msup><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo fence="false">|</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle u^{*}_{1^{-}}(x)=\mathbb{E}_{x_{t}\sim p_{t|1}(x_{t}|x)}[\frac{x-x_{t}}{1-t}]=\frac{\mathbb{E}_{x_{t}\sim p_{t}}[\frac{x-x_{t}}{1-t}k_{t}(x,x_{t})]}{\mathbb{E}_{x_{t}\sim p_{t}}[k_{t}(x,x_{t})]}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.Thmtheorem1.p1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.Thmtheorem1.p1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">see <a href="#A1.SS3" title="A.3 Proof of ‣ Appendix A Missing Proofs and Theorems ‣ A Long-Short Flow-Map Perspective for Drifting Models" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">subsection A.3</span></a> for proof.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">In the above formulation, <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> does not admit a closed-form expression. We therefore approximate it using samples pushed forward by the learned long flow map, i.e., <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{t}\approx\psi_{0\to t}^{\theta}(x_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>≈</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ψ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{t}\approx\psi_{0\to t}^{\theta}(x_{0})</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{0}\sim p_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{0}\sim p_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>. Moreover, although the theorem states <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lim_{t\to 1^{-}}u_{t}^{*}(x)=x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>lim</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mrow><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lim_{t\to 1^{-}}u_{t}^{*}(x)=x</annotation></semantics></math>, directly setting <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{1^{-}}(x)=x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><msup><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{1^{-}}(x)=x</annotation></semantics></math> is insufficient: it does not cancel the <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta t</annotation></semantics></math> terms (which is crucial in the derivation of <a href="#S3.E12" title="Equation 12 ‣ 3.1 First-Order Approximation ‣ 3 Long-Short Flow-Map Perspective ‣ A Long-Short Flow-Map Perspective for Drifting Models" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Equation 12</span></a>) and it cannot reflect the discrepancy between <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>. We therefore adopt the Flow Matching closed-form solution of the instantaneous velocity <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{1-\Delta t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{1-\Delta t}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{1^{-}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>u</mi><msup><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo></msup></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{1^{-}}</annotation></semantics></math> at <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=1-\Delta t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=1-\Delta t</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t=1</annotation></semantics></math></p>
<table id="S3.E16" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="S3.E16X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E16X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E16X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{x_{0}\sim p_{0}}\Big[\|\psi^{\theta}_{0\to 1}(x_{0})-sg\big(\psi^{\theta}_{0\to 1-\Delta t}(x_{0})+\frac{1}{2}\Delta tu_{1-\Delta t}(x^{\theta}_{1-\Delta t})+\frac{1}{2}\Delta tu_{1^{-}}(x_{1}^{\theta})\big)\|^{2}\Big]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>ψ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>ψ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><msup><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{x_{0}\sim p_{0}}\Big[\|\psi^{\theta}_{0\to 1}(x_{0})-sg\big(\psi^{\theta}_{0\to 1-\Delta t}(x_{0})+\frac{1}{2}\Delta tu_{1-\Delta t}(x^{\theta}_{1-\Delta t})+\frac{1}{2}\Delta tu_{1^{-}}(x_{1}^{\theta})\big)\|^{2}\Big]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="5" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S3.E16Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E16Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{x_{0}\sim p_{0}}\Big[\|\psi^{\theta}_{0\to 1}(x_{0})-sg\big(\psi^{\theta}_{0\to 1-\Delta t}(x_{0})+\frac{1}{2}\Delta t\frac{\mathbb{E}_{x_{1}\sim p_{1}}[\frac{x_{1}-\psi^{\theta}_{0\to 1-\Delta t}(x_{0})}{1-({1-\Delta t})}k^{\epsilon}_{1-\Delta t}(x_{1},\psi^{\theta}_{0\to 1-\Delta t}(x_{0}))]}{\mathbb{E}_{x_{1}\sim p_{1}}[k^{\epsilon}_{1-\Delta t}(x_{1},\psi^{\theta}_{0\to 1-\Delta t}(x_{0}))]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>ψ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi><mi>g</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>ψ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>t</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ψ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>k</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mi>ϵ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ψ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>k</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mi>ϵ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ψ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{x_{0}\sim p_{0}}\Big[\|\psi^{\theta}_{0\to 1}(x_{0})-sg\big(\psi^{\theta}_{0\to 1-\Delta t}(x_{0})+\frac{1}{2}\Delta t\frac{\mathbb{E}_{x_{1}\sim p_{1}}[\frac{x_{1}-\psi^{\theta}_{0\to 1-\Delta t}(x_{0})}{1-({1-\Delta t})}k^{\epsilon}_{1-\Delta t}(x_{1},\psi^{\theta}_{0\to 1-\Delta t}(x_{0}))]}{\mathbb{E}_{x_{1}\sim p_{1}}[k^{\epsilon}_{1-\Delta t}(x_{1},\psi^{\theta}_{0\to 1-\Delta t}(x_{0}))]}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="S3.E16Xb" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E16Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+\frac{1}{2}\Delta t\frac{\mathbb{E}_{x^{\theta}_{1-\Delta t}\sim p^{\theta}_{1-\Delta t}}[\frac{\psi^{\theta}_{0\to 1}(x_{0})-x_{1-\Delta t}^{\theta}}{1-(1-\Delta t)}k^{\epsilon}_{1-\Delta t}(\psi^{\theta}_{0\to 1}(x_{0}),x_{1-\Delta t}^{\theta})]}{\mathbb{E}_{x^{\theta}_{1-\Delta t}\sim p^{\theta}_{1-\Delta t}}[k^{\epsilon}_{1-\Delta t}(\psi^{\theta}_{0\to 1}(x_{0}),x_{1-\Delta t}^{\theta})]}\big)\|^{2}\Big]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mi>t</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo>∼</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msubsup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>ψ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msubsup></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>k</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mi>ϵ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ψ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo>∼</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msubsup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>k</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mi>ϵ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ψ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\frac{1}{2}\Delta t\frac{\mathbb{E}_{x^{\theta}_{1-\Delta t}\sim p^{\theta}_{1-\Delta t}}[\frac{\psi^{\theta}_{0\to 1}(x_{0})-x_{1-\Delta t}^{\theta}}{1-(1-\Delta t)}k^{\epsilon}_{1-\Delta t}(\psi^{\theta}_{0\to 1}(x_{0}),x_{1-\Delta t}^{\theta})]}{\mathbb{E}_{x^{\theta}_{1-\Delta t}\sim p^{\theta}_{1-\Delta t}}[k^{\epsilon}_{1-\Delta t}(\psi^{\theta}_{0\to 1}(x_{0}),x_{1-\Delta t}^{\theta})]}\big)\|^{2}\Big]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="S3.E16Xc" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E16Xc.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{x_{0}\sim p_{0}}\Big[\|\psi^{\theta}_{0\to 1}(x_{0})-sg\big(\psi^{\theta}_{0\to 1-\Delta t}(x_{0})+\frac{1}{2}\frac{\mathbb{E}_{x_{1}\sim p_{1}}[(x_{1}-\psi^{\theta}_{0\to 1-\Delta t}(x_{0}))k^{\epsilon}_{1-\Delta t}(x_{1},\psi^{\theta}_{0\to 1-\Delta t}(x_{0}))]}{\mathbb{E}_{x_{1}\sim p_{1}}[k^{\epsilon}_{1-\Delta t}(x_{1},\psi^{\theta}_{0\to 1-\Delta t}(x_{0}))]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>ψ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi><mi>g</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>ψ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ψ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>k</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mi>ϵ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ψ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>k</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mi>ϵ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ψ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{x_{0}\sim p_{0}}\Big[\|\psi^{\theta}_{0\to 1}(x_{0})-sg\big(\psi^{\theta}_{0\to 1-\Delta t}(x_{0})+\frac{1}{2}\frac{\mathbb{E}_{x_{1}\sim p_{1}}[(x_{1}-\psi^{\theta}_{0\to 1-\Delta t}(x_{0}))k^{\epsilon}_{1-\Delta t}(x_{1},\psi^{\theta}_{0\to 1-\Delta t}(x_{0}))]}{\mathbb{E}_{x_{1}\sim p_{1}}[k^{\epsilon}_{1-\Delta t}(x_{1},\psi^{\theta}_{0\to 1-\Delta t}(x_{0}))]}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="S3.E16Xd" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E16Xd.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+\frac{1}{2}\frac{\mathbb{E}_{x^{\theta}_{1-\Delta t}\sim p^{\theta}_{1-\Delta t}}[(\psi_{0\to 1}^{\theta}(x_{0})-x_{1-\Delta t}^{\theta})k^{\epsilon}_{1-\Delta t}(\psi_{0\to 1}^{\theta}(x_{0}),x_{1-\Delta t}^{\theta})]}{\mathbb{E}_{x^{\theta}_{1-\Delta t}\sim p^{\theta}_{1-\Delta t}}[k^{\epsilon}_{1-\Delta t}(\psi_{0\to 1}^{\theta}(x_{0}),x_{1-\Delta t}^{\theta})]}\big)\|^{2}\Big]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo>∼</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msubsup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>ψ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>k</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mi>ϵ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ψ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo>∼</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msubsup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>k</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mi>ϵ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ψ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\frac{1}{2}\frac{\mathbb{E}_{x^{\theta}_{1-\Delta t}\sim p^{\theta}_{1-\Delta t}}[(\psi_{0\to 1}^{\theta}(x_{0})-x_{1-\Delta t}^{\theta})k^{\epsilon}_{1-\Delta t}(\psi_{0\to 1}^{\theta}(x_{0}),x_{1-\Delta t}^{\theta})]}{\mathbb{E}_{x^{\theta}_{1-\Delta t}\sim p^{\theta}_{1-\Delta t}}[k^{\epsilon}_{1-\Delta t}(\psi_{0\to 1}^{\theta}(x_{0}),x_{1-\Delta t}^{\theta})]}\big)\|^{2}\Big]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.p2.3" class="ltx_p">where we denote the distribution of <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{\theta}_{1-\Delta t}=\psi^{\theta}_{0\to 1-\Delta t}(x^{\prime}_{0}),x^{\prime}_{0}\sim p_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ψ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{\theta}_{1-\Delta t}=\psi^{\theta}_{0\to 1-\Delta t}(x^{\prime}_{0}),x^{\prime}_{0}\sim p_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> as <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x^{\theta}_{1-\Delta t}\sim p_{1-\Delta t}^{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo>∼</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x^{\theta}_{1-\Delta t}\sim p_{1-\Delta t}^{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then let <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta t\to 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta t\to 0</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</p>
<table id="S3.E17" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="S3.E17X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E17X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E17X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{x_{0}\sim p_{0}}\Big[\|\psi^{\theta}_{0\to 1}(x_{0})-sg\big(\psi^{\theta}_{0\to 1}(x_{0})+\frac{1}{2}\frac{\mathbb{E}_{x_{1}\sim p_{1}}[(x_{1}-\psi^{\theta}_{0\to 1}(x_{0}))k^{\epsilon}_{1}(x_{1},\psi^{\theta}_{0\to 1}(x_{0}))]}{\mathbb{E}_{x_{1}\sim p_{1}}[k^{\epsilon}_{1}(x_{1},\psi^{\theta}_{0\to 1}(x_{0}))]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>𝔼</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>ψ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi><mi>g</mi><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mi>ψ</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ψ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>k</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>ϵ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ψ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>k</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>ϵ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ψ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{x_{0}\sim p_{0}}\Big[\|\psi^{\theta}_{0\to 1}(x_{0})-sg\big(\psi^{\theta}_{0\to 1}(x_{0})+\frac{1}{2}\frac{\mathbb{E}_{x_{1}\sim p_{1}}[(x_{1}-\psi^{\theta}_{0\to 1}(x_{0}))k^{\epsilon}_{1}(x_{1},\psi^{\theta}_{0\to 1}(x_{0}))]}{\mathbb{E}_{x_{1}\sim p_{1}}[k^{\epsilon}_{1}(x_{1},\psi^{\theta}_{0\to 1}(x_{0}))]}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(17)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S3.E17Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E17Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+\frac{1}{2}\frac{\mathbb{E}_{x^{\theta}_{1}=\psi_{0\to 1}^{\theta}(x^{\prime}_{0}),x^{\prime}_{0}\sim p_{0}}[(\psi_{0\to 1}^{\theta}(x_{0})-x_{1}^{\theta})k^{\epsilon}_{1}(\psi_{0\to 1}^{\theta}(x_{0}),x_{1}^{\theta})]}{\mathbb{E}_{x^{\theta}_{1}=\psi_{0\to 1}^{\theta}(x^{\prime}_{0}),x^{\prime}_{0}\sim p_{0}}[k^{\epsilon}_{1}(\psi_{0\to 1}^{\theta}(x_{0}),x_{1}^{\theta})]}\big)\|^{2}\Big]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ψ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>ψ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>θ</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>k</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>ϵ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ψ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ψ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>k</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>ϵ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ψ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\frac{1}{2}\frac{\mathbb{E}_{x^{\theta}_{1}=\psi_{0\to 1}^{\theta}(x^{\prime}_{0}),x^{\prime}_{0}\sim p_{0}}[(\psi_{0\to 1}^{\theta}(x_{0})-x_{1}^{\theta})k^{\epsilon}_{1}(\psi_{0\to 1}^{\theta}(x_{0}),x_{1}^{\theta})]}{\mathbb{E}_{x^{\theta}_{1}=\psi_{0\to 1}^{\theta}(x^{\prime}_{0}),x^{\prime}_{0}\sim p_{0}}[k^{\epsilon}_{1}(\psi_{0\to 1}^{\theta}(x_{0}),x_{1}^{\theta})]}\big)\|^{2}\Big]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS2.p2.4" class="ltx_p">In this loss, the trapezoidal-rule approximation of the short flow map provides a more accurate supervisory signal for learning the long flow map. Compared to the first-order Euler-based objective in <a href="#S3.E13" title="Equation 13 ‣ 3.1 First-Order Approximation ‣ 3 Long-Short Flow-Map Perspective ‣ A Long-Short Flow-Map Perspective for Drifting Models" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Equation 13</span></a>, the key difference lies in the residual term: it is no longer a point-to-distribution regression target between point <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi_{0\to 1}^{\theta}(x_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>ψ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi_{0\to 1}^{\theta}(x_{0})</annotation></semantics></math> and distribution <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>, but rather a discrepancy between two distributions <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{1}^{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{1}^{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> estimated from samples <math id="S3.SS2.p2.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi_{0\to 1}^{\theta}(x_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>ψ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi_{0\to 1}^{\theta}(x_{0})</annotation></semantics></math>. As a result, when the flow map is optimal, the residual does not merely attain a regression-optimal value; it becomes exactly zero.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">3.3 </span>Connection with Drifting Model</h3>

<div id="S3.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In the derivation above, we use the long-short flow-map decomposition to combine flow-map learning with the Flow-Matching closed-form solution: the closed-form solution on the short flow map provides a dataset-tied supervisory signal, enabling learning the long flow map and yielding a one-step map <math id="S3.SS3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi^{\theta}_{0\to 1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>ψ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi^{\theta}_{0\to 1}</annotation></semantics></math>. From this perspective, the objectives in <a href="#S3.E13" title="Equation 13 ‣ 3.1 First-Order Approximation ‣ 3 Long-Short Flow-Map Perspective ‣ A Long-Short Flow-Map Perspective for Drifting Models" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Equation 13</span></a> and <a href="#S3.E17" title="Equation 17 ‣ 3.2 Second-Order Approximation ‣ 3 Long-Short Flow-Map Perspective ‣ A Long-Short Flow-Map Perspective for Drifting Models" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Equation 17</span></a> recover the losses used in the Drifting Model <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">Deng et al. (2026)</a></cite>. This connection provides a principled derivation of the Drifting Model and enables intuitive explanations of its key design choices. We first summarize the Drifting Model and then elaborate on its connection to our derivation by showing how its training objectives and design choices naturally arise from the long-short flow-map viewpoint.</p>
</div>
<section id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Drifting Model</h5>

<div id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The Drifting Model <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">Deng et al. (2026)</a></cite> directly learns a one-step mapping <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{\theta}:\mathcal{X}\to\mathcal{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mi>θ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{\theta}:\mathcal{X}\to\mathcal{X}</annotation></semantics></math> that pushes forward noise to data, i.e., <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{\theta}(\epsilon)\sim q_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mi>θ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{\theta}(\epsilon)\sim q_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon\sim p_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon\sim p_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, and aims to match <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{1}=p_{\text{data}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mtext>data</mtext></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{1}=p_{\text{data}}</annotation></semantics></math>. The main idea is to make the pushforward distribution progressively closer to the target distribution during training. Specifically, the method introduces a drift field <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{p_{1},q_{\theta}}:\mathcal{X}\to\mathcal{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{p_{1},q_{\theta}}:\mathcal{X}\to\mathcal{X}</annotation></semantics></math> that corrects samples from <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> toward <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> and ideally satisfies <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x+V_{p,q_{\theta}}(x)\sim p_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x+V_{p,q_{\theta}}(x)\sim p_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> when <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\sim q_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\sim q_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>. Training then encourages <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{\theta}(\epsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mi>θ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{\theta}(\epsilon)</annotation></semantics></math> to agree with its drift-corrected counterpart:</p>
<table id="S3.E18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}(\theta)=\mathbb{E}_{\epsilon\sim p_{0}}\Big[\big\|f^{\theta}(\epsilon)-\mathrm{sg}\!\big(f^{\theta}(\epsilon)+V_{p_{1},q_{\theta}}(f^{\theta}(\epsilon))\big)\big\|_{2}^{2}\Big]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>ϵ</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mi>θ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.812em;" width="0.812em"><mi>sg</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mi>θ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mi>θ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em" stretchy="true">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}(\theta)=\mathbb{E}_{\epsilon\sim p_{0}}\Big[\big\|f^{\theta}(\epsilon)-\mathrm{sg}\!\big(f^{\theta}(\epsilon)+V_{p_{1},q_{\theta}}(f^{\theta}(\epsilon))\big)\big\|_{2}^{2}\Big],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(18)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="q_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>q</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">q_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the distribution induced by <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f^{\theta}(\epsilon)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mi>θ</mi></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϵ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f^{\theta}(\epsilon)</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">For <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{p,q}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{p,q}</annotation></semantics></math> that incorporates supervision from the target data distribution, the Drifting Model adopts a kernel-based construction with an attraction-repulsion structure:</p>
<table id="S3.E19" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="S3.E19X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E19X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle V_{p,q}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle V_{p,q}(x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E19X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=V_{p}^{+}(x)-V_{q}^{-}(x)," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=V_{p}^{+}(x)-V_{q}^{-}(x),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="3" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(19)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S3.E19Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E19Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle V_{p}^{+}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle V_{p}^{+}(x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E19Xa.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\mathbb{E}_{y\sim p}[k(x,y)(y-x)]}{\mathbb{E}_{y\sim p}[k(x,y)]}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>p</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\mathbb{E}_{y\sim p}[k(x,y)(y-x)]}{\mathbb{E}_{y\sim p}[k(x,y)]},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="S3.E19Xb" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E19Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle V_{q}^{-}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle V_{q}^{-}(x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E19Xb.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{\mathbb{E}_{y\sim q}[k(x,y)(y-x)]}{\mathbb{E}_{y\sim q}[k(x,y)]}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{\mathbb{E}_{y\sim q}[k(x,y)(y-x)]}{\mathbb{E}_{y\sim q}[k(x,y)]},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k(x,y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k(x,y)</annotation></semantics></math> is a similarity kernel (implemented via a Laplacian kernel <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="e^{-\|y-x\|/\epsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">−</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∥</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∥</mo><mo lspace="0em">/</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{-\|y-x\|/\epsilon}</annotation></semantics></math> in practice). Ideally, this definition satisfies a consistency condition: <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{p,q}(x)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{p,q}(x)=0</annotation></semantics></math> whenever <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p=q" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p=q</annotation></semantics></math>, so that no correction is applied when the two distributions coincide.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Connection of Loss Functions</h5>

<div id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We observe that the loss in <a href="#S3.E13" title="Equation 13 ‣ 3.1 First-Order Approximation ‣ 3 Long-Short Flow-Map Perspective ‣ A Long-Short Flow-Map Perspective for Drifting Models" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Equation 13</span></a> obtained by approximating the short terminal evolution via a first-order forward Euler step coincides with the Drifting Model objective that uses the attraction-only drift field <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{p,q}(x)=V_{p}^{+}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{p,q}(x)=V_{p}^{+}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> for the drifting loss in <a href="#S3.E18" title="Equation 18 ‣ Drifting Model ‣ 3.3 Connection with Drifting Model ‣ 3 Long-Short Flow-Map Perspective ‣ A Long-Short Flow-Map Perspective for Drifting Models" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Equation 18</span></a>, where</p>
<table id="S3.E20" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="S3.E20X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E20X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle f^{\theta}\coloneqq\psi_{0\to 1}^{\theta},\qquad V_{p_{1},p_{1}^{\theta}}=V_{p_{1}}^{+},\qquad V_{p_{1}}^{+}(x)=\frac{\mathbb{E}_{x_{1}\sim p_{1}}[(x_{1}-x)k_{1}(x_{1},x)]}{\mathbb{E}_{x_{1}\sim p_{1}}[k_{1}(x_{1},x)]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mi>θ</mi></msup><mo>≔</mo><msubsup><mi>ψ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>θ</mi></msubsup></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="2.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle f^{\theta}\coloneqq\psi_{0\to 1}^{\theta},\qquad V_{p_{1},p_{1}^{\theta}}=V_{p_{1}}^{+},\qquad V_{p_{1}}^{+}(x)=\frac{\mathbb{E}_{x_{1}\sim p_{1}}[(x_{1}-x)k_{1}(x_{1},x)]}{\mathbb{E}_{x_{1}\sim p_{1}}[k_{1}(x_{1},x)]}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(20)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">In contrast, the loss in <a href="#S3.E17" title="Equation 17 ‣ 3.2 Second-Order Approximation ‣ 3 Long-Short Flow-Map Perspective ‣ A Long-Short Flow-Map Perspective for Drifting Models" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Equation 17</span></a> derived from a second-order trapezoidal approximation over the same short interval matches the Drifting Model objective with the attraction-repulsion drift field <math id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V_{p,q}(x)=V_{p}^{+}(x)-V_{q}^{-}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>p</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>q</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>q</mi><mo>−</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V_{p,q}(x)=V_{p}^{+}(x)-V_{q}^{-}(x)</annotation></semantics></math>, where</p>
<table id="S3.E21" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="S3.E21X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.E21X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle f^{\theta}\coloneqq\psi_{0\to 1}^{\theta},\quad V_{p_{1},p_{1}^{\theta}}=V_{p_{1}}^{+}-V_{p_{1}^{\theta}}^{-},\quad V_{p_{1}}^{+}(x)=\frac{\mathbb{E}_{x_{1}\sim p_{1}}[(x_{1}-x)k_{1}(x_{1},x)]}{\mathbb{E}_{x_{1}\sim p_{1}}[k_{1}(x_{1},x)]},\quad V_{p_{1}^{\theta}}^{-}(x)=\frac{\mathbb{E}_{x_{1}\sim p^{\theta}_{1}}[(x_{1}-x)k_{1}(x,x_{1})]}{\mathbb{E}_{x_{1}\sim p^{\theta}_{1}}[k_{1}(x,x_{1})]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>f</mi><mi>θ</mi></msup><mo>≔</mo><msubsup><mi>ψ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>θ</mi></msubsup></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>V</mi><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo>−</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>θ</mi></msubsup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>θ</mi></msubsup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle f^{\theta}\coloneqq\psi_{0\to 1}^{\theta},\quad V_{p_{1},p_{1}^{\theta}}=V_{p_{1}}^{+}-V_{p_{1}^{\theta}}^{-},\quad V_{p_{1}}^{+}(x)=\frac{\mathbb{E}_{x_{1}\sim p_{1}}[(x_{1}-x)k_{1}(x_{1},x)]}{\mathbb{E}_{x_{1}\sim p_{1}}[k_{1}(x_{1},x)]},\quad V_{p_{1}^{\theta}}^{-}(x)=\frac{\mathbb{E}_{x_{1}\sim p^{\theta}_{1}}[(x_{1}-x)k_{1}(x,x_{1})]}{\mathbb{E}_{x_{1}\sim p^{\theta}_{1}}[k_{1}(x,x_{1})]}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(21)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Discussion on Design Choices</h5>

<div id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The connection between the loss functions yields the following insights regarding several design choices of the Drifting Model, which we will discuss briefly below.</p>
<ol id="S3.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="S3.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="S3.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Interpretation. The Drifting Model can be viewed as learning a flow map via trajectory consistency, and then selecting the segment <math id="S3.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s\to r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s\to r</annotation></semantics></math> in <a href="#S2.Thmtheorem3" title="Proposition 2.3 (Trajectory Consistency). ‣ 2.2 One-Step Flow Map ‣ 2 Background ‣ A Long-Short Flow-Map Perspective for Drifting Models" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Proposition 2.3</span></a> to be a very short interval near the terminal time, i.e., <math id="S3.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\Delta t\to 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\Delta t\to 1</annotation></semantics></math>. Over this short interval, it directly applies the closed-form solution of Flow Matching to obtain supervision from the dataset.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="S3.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Why <math id="S3.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V^{+}-V^{-}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>−</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V^{+}-V^{-}</annotation></semantics></math> emerges and why it helps. If the estimation over <math id="S3.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\Delta t\to 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\Delta t\to 1</annotation></semantics></math> uses a first-order forward Euler method, one recovers the original Drifting Model form that involves only <math id="S3.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V^{+}</annotation></semantics></math>. In contrast, if a second-order trapezoidal rule is used, the derivation naturally yields the balanced attraction–repulsion form <math id="S3.I1.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V^{+}-V^{-}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>−</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V^{+}-V^{-}</annotation></semantics></math>. Since the learned flow map is generally not optimal, the terminal interval <math id="S3.I1.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\Delta t\to 1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\Delta t\to 1</annotation></semantics></math> remains affected by approximation error even as <math id="S3.I1.i2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\Delta t\to 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Delta t\to 0</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, the order of the terminal-interval estimator provides a principled explanation for why the symmetric correction <math id="S3.I1.i2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V^{+}-V^{-}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>−</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V^{+}-V^{-}</annotation></semantics></math> tends to outperform the one-sided variant <math id="S3.I1.i2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="V^{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>+</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">V^{+}</annotation></semantics></math>, as well as other imbalanced choices such as <math id="S3.I1.i2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3V^{+}-V^{-}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></mrow><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>V</mi><mo>−</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3V^{+}-V^{-}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S3.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="S3.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Kernel Selection. As revealed by the proofs of <a href="#A1.SS1" title="A.1 Proof of ‣ Appendix A Missing Proofs and Theorems ‣ A Long-Short Flow-Map Perspective for Drifting Models" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">subsection A.1</span></a> and <a href="#A1.SS3" title="A.3 Proof of ‣ Appendix A Missing Proofs and Theorems ‣ A Long-Short Flow-Map Perspective for Drifting Models" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">subsection A.3</span></a>, the kernel <math id="S3.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{t}(x,y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{t}(x,y)</annotation></semantics></math> adopted in <a href="#S3.E13" title="Equation 13 ‣ 3.1 First-Order Approximation ‣ 3 Long-Short Flow-Map Perspective ‣ A Long-Short Flow-Map Perspective for Drifting Models" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Equation 13</span></a> and <a href="#S3.E17" title="Equation 17 ‣ 3.2 Second-Order Approximation ‣ 3 Long-Short Flow-Map Perspective ‣ A Long-Short Flow-Map Perspective for Drifting Models" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Equation 17</span></a> is tightly coupled with the form of the initial noise distribution <math id="S3.I1.i3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>. In particular, when we choose Gaussian noise, the resulting kernel naturally becomes the squared-exponential Gaussian kernel <math id="S3.I1.i3.p1.m3" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="e^{-|y-x|^{2}/\epsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">−</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><msup><mrow></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em">/</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{-|y-x|^{2}/\epsilon}</annotation></semantics></math>. Importantly, our framework does not restrict the choice of <math id="S3.I1.i3.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>, and therefore does not constrain the kernel family in <a href="#S3.E13" title="Equation 13 ‣ 3.1 First-Order Approximation ‣ 3 Long-Short Flow-Map Perspective ‣ A Long-Short Flow-Map Perspective for Drifting Models" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Equation 13</span></a> and <a href="#S3.E17" title="Equation 17 ‣ 3.2 Second-Order Approximation ‣ 3 Long-Short Flow-Map Perspective ‣ A Long-Short Flow-Map Perspective for Drifting Models" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Equation 17</span></a> either. For example, by choosing <math id="S3.I1.i3.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{0}</annotation></semantics></math> to follow a Laplace distribution, we recover the Laplacian kernel <math id="S3.I1.i3.p1.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="e^{-|y-x|/\epsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>e</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0em">−</mo><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>y</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><mo lspace="0em">/</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e^{-|y-x|/\epsilon}</annotation></semantics></math> used in the original Drifting Model <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">Deng et al. (2026)</a></cite>. More broadly, relating kernel design to the choice of initial noise indicates a connection between these two components. This connection hints that recent advances in initial-noise optimization, such as blue-noise sampling strategies <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib12" title="" class="ltx_ref">Huang et al. (2024)</a></cite>, could be incorporated to refine the kernel selections in <a href="#S3.E13" title="Equation 13 ‣ 3.1 First-Order Approximation ‣ 3 Long-Short Flow-Map Perspective ‣ A Long-Short Flow-Map Perspective for Drifting Models" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Equation 13</span></a> and <a href="#S3.E17" title="Equation 17 ‣ 3.2 Second-Order Approximation ‣ 3 Long-Short Flow-Map Perspective ‣ A Long-Short Flow-Map Perspective for Drifting Models" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Equation 17</span></a>. A systematic investigation of this direction remains open.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
<p id="S3.SS3.SSS0.Px3.p1.2" class="ltx_p">In <a href="#A3" title="Appendix C Discussion on Classifier-Free Guidance ‣ A Long-Short Flow-Map Perspective for Drifting Models" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Appendix C</span></a>, we discuss classifier-free guidance (CFG), which <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">Deng et al. (2026)</a></cite> identifies as a key distinction between Drifting Model and distribution moment matching <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib13" title="" class="ltx_ref">Li et al. (2015)</a>; <a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">Dziugaite et al. (2015)</a></cite> (see the related-work discussion in <a href="#S7" title="7 Related Work ‣ A Long-Short Flow-Map Perspective for Drifting Models" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">section 7</span></a>).</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S4" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">4 </span>Application: Likelihood Learning</h2>

<div id="S4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Here we leverage the long-short flow-map perspective to derive a new objective for learning data likelihoods.</p>
</div>
<section id="S4.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.1 </span>Background</h3>

<div id="S4.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">For one-step generative methods based on flow maps, one can in principle compute the likelihood using the learned map <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi_{t\to r}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi_{t\to r}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> via the change-of-variables formula <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log p_{r}(x_{r})=\log p_{t}(x_{t})-\log|\det\frac{\partial\psi_{t\to r}(x)}{\partial x}|_{x=x_{t}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">det</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log p_{r}(x_{r})=\log p_{t}(x_{t})-\log|\det\frac{\partial\psi_{t\to r}(x)}{\partial x}|_{x=x_{t}}</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{r}=\psi_{t\to r}(x_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{r}=\psi_{t\to r}(x_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>. However, this requires evaluating the Jacobian determinant of the flow map, which does not scale to high-dimensional data. To address this issue, <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ai et al. (2025)</a></cite> proposes to jointly learn, together with the flow map <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi^{\theta}_{t\to r}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>ψ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi^{\theta}_{t\to r}(x)</annotation></semantics></math>, an auxiliary model <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D^{\theta}_{t\to r}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D^{\theta}_{t\to r}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> that predicts the average likelihood change from time <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math> to <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>r</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r</annotation></semantics></math>, namely <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{t\to r}(x)=\frac{\log p_{r}(\psi_{t\to r}(x))-\log p_{t}(x)}{r-t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{t\to r}(x)=\frac{\log p_{r}(\psi_{t\to r}(x))-\log p_{t}(x)}{r-t}</annotation></semantics></math> . Concretely, the evolution of the log-likelihood quantity <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log p_{r}(\psi_{t\to r}(x))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log p_{r}(\psi_{t\to r}(x))</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies</p>
<table id="S4.E22" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="S4.E22X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E22X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{\partial\log p_{r}(\psi_{t\to r}(x))}{\partial r}=-\nabla\cdot u_{r}(y)|_{y=\psi_{t\to r}(x)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∂</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mo>∇</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>u</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>r</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo fence="false" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mrow></mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{\partial\log p_{r}(\psi_{t\to r}(x))}{\partial r}=-\nabla\cdot u_{r}(y)|_{y=\psi_{t\to r}(x)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(22)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS1.p1.3" class="ltx_p">and <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{t\to r}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{t\to r}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies a trajectory consistency property <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(r-t)D_{t\to r}(x_{t})=(r-s)D_{s\to r}(x_{s})+(s-t)D_{t\to s}(x_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(r-t)D_{t\to r}(x_{t})=(r-s)D_{s\to r}(x_{s})+(s-t)D_{t\to s}(x_{t})</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{s}=\psi_{t\to s}(x_{t})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>s</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{s}=\psi_{t\to s}(x_{t})</annotation></semantics></math> for arbitrary <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t&lt;s&lt;r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t&lt;s&lt;r</annotation></semantics></math>. Using this trajectory consistency and the evolution <a href="#S4.E22" title="Equation 22 ‣ 4.1 Background ‣ 4 Application: Likelihood Learning ‣ A Long-Short Flow-Map Perspective for Drifting Models" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Equation 22</span></a> as a boundary condition <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m14" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="D_{t\to t}(x)=-\nabla\cdot u_{t}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mo>∇</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{t\to t}(x)=-\nabla\cdot u_{t}(x)</annotation></semantics></math>, <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ai et al. (2025)</a></cite> learns <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D_{t\to r}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D_{t\to r}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> jointly with the flow map <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi_{t\to r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi_{t\to r}</annotation></semantics></math>. With the learned <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D^{\theta}_{t\to r}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D^{\theta}_{t\to r}(x)</annotation></semantics></math>, for any generated sample <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x_{1}=\psi_{0\to 1}(x_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x_{1}=\psi_{0\to 1}(x_{0})</annotation></semantics></math>, one can efficiently obtain its likelihood <math id="S4.SS1.p1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log p_{1}(x_{1})=\log p_{0}(x_{0})+D^{\theta}_{0\to 1}(x_{0})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log p_{1}(x_{1})=\log p_{0}(x_{0})+D^{\theta}_{0\to 1}(x_{0})</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">4.2 </span>Drifting Model for Likelihood Learning</h3>

<div id="S4.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We aim to derive an analogous likelihood-learning objective for the Drifting Model under our flow-map perspective. Different from <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib15" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ai et al. (2025)</a></cite>, our goal is to learn the Eulerian log-likelihood change <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{t\to r}(x)=\log p_{r}(x)-\log p_{t}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{t\to r}(x)=\log p_{r}(x)-\log p_{t}(x)</annotation></semantics></math>.
When combined with the flow map <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi_{t\to r}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi_{t\to r}</annotation></semantics></math>, the composed quantity <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{t\to r}(\psi_{t\to r}(x))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{t\to r}(\psi_{t\to r}(x))</annotation></semantics></math> can also play a Lagrangian role. In the Eulerian view, <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log p_{t}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log p_{t}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> satisfies the following evolution equation</p>
<table id="S4.E23" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="S4.E23X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E23X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\frac{\partial}{\partial t}\log p_{t}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\frac{\partial}{\partial t}\log p_{t}(x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E23X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-\nabla\log p_{t}(x)\cdot u_{t}(x)-\nabla\cdot u_{t}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>p</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>u</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo><mo>−</mo><mo>∇</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>u</mi><msub><mrow></mrow><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\nabla\log p_{t}(x)\cdot u_{t}(x)-\nabla\cdot u_{t}(x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(23)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p1.2" class="ltx_p">Because <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{t\to r}(x)=\log p_{r}(x)-\log p_{t}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>r</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{t\to r}(x)=\log p_{r}(x)-\log p_{t}(x)</annotation></semantics></math>, it satisfies the evolution equation <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\frac{\partial}{\partial r}G_{t\to r}(x)=-\nabla\log p_{r}(x)\cdot u_{r}(x)-\nabla\cdot u_{r}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac><mo>∂</mo><mrow><mo>∂</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></mfrac><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mo>∇</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>r</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\partial}{\partial r}G_{t\to r}(x)=-\nabla\log p_{r}(x)\cdot u_{r}(x)-\nabla\cdot u_{r}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> and the consistency relation <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{t\to r}(x)=G_{s\to r}(x)+G_{t\to s}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{t\to r}(x)=G_{s\to r}(x)+G_{t\to s}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> for arbitrary <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t&lt;s&lt;r" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>s</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t&lt;s&lt;r</annotation></semantics></math>. Following the same idea as before, we apply this relation on <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[0,1]</annotation></semantics></math> with a split point <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\Delta t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\Delta t</annotation></semantics></math>, namely <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{0\to 1}(x)=G_{0\to 1-\Delta t}(x)+G_{1-\Delta t\to 1}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{0\to 1}(x)=G_{0\to 1-\Delta t}(x)+G_{1-\Delta t\to 1}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> and approximate <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{1-\Delta t\to 1}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>G</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{1-\Delta t\to 1}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> by the trapezoidal rule. For the learned flow map <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi_{t\to r}^{\theta}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>ψ</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi_{t\to r}^{\theta}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> and the learned likelihood change <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G_{t\to r}^{\theta}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>G</mi><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G_{t\to r}^{\theta}(x)</annotation></semantics></math>, we enforce that they satisfy</p>
<table id="S4.E24" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="S4.E24X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E24X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle G^{\theta}_{0\to 1}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>G</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle G^{\theta}_{0\to 1}(x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E24X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\approx G^{\theta}_{0\to 1-\Delta t}(x)-\frac{\Delta t}{2}(\nabla\log p^{\theta}_{1-\Delta t}(x)u_{1-\Delta t}(x)+\nabla\log p^{\theta}_{1}(x)u_{1^{-}}(x)+\nabla\cdot u_{1^{-}}(x)+\nabla\cdot u_{1-\Delta t}(x))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≈</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>G</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>log</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>log</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>θ</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><msup><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>∇</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><msup><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>∇</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\approx G^{\theta}_{0\to 1-\Delta t}(x)-\frac{\Delta t}{2}(\nabla\log p^{\theta}_{1-\Delta t}(x)u_{1-\Delta t}(x)+\nabla\log p^{\theta}_{1}(x)u_{1^{-}}(x)+\nabla\cdot u_{1^{-}}(x)+\nabla\cdot u_{1-\Delta t}(x))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(24)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS2.p1.3" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{t}^{\theta}(x)=p_{0}(x)e^{G_{0\to t}^{\theta}(x)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msubsup><mi>G</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{t}^{\theta}(x)=p_{0}(x)e^{G_{0\to t}^{\theta}(x)}</annotation></semantics></math>. Here, we need to compute the divergence terms <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla\cdot u_{1-\Delta t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>∇</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla\cdot u_{1-\Delta t}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS2.p1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla\cdot u_{1^{-}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>∇</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><msup><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo></msup></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla\cdot u_{1^{-}}</annotation></semantics></math>, whose evaluation is provided by the following theorem.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_theorem">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Theorem 4.1</span></span><span id="S4.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Closed-Form Solution for Velocity Divergence)<span id="S4.Thmtheorem1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">For the closed-form solution of the velocity field <math id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u^{*}_{t}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u^{*}_{t}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> in <a href="#S2.E5" title="Equation 5 ‣ Theorem 2.1 (Closed-Form Solution of Flow Matching ( ) ). ‣ 2.1 Closed-Form Flow Matching ‣ 2 Background ‣ A Long-Short Flow-Map Perspective for Drifting Models" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Equation 5</span></a> and the endpoint velocity <math id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u^{*}_{1^{-}}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>u</mi><msup><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo></msup><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u^{*}_{1^{-}}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> in <a href="#S3.E15" title="Equation 15 ‣ Theorem 3.1 (Closed-Form Solution of the Endpoint Velocity). ‣ 3.2 Second-Order Approximation ‣ 3 Long-Short Flow-Map Perspective ‣ A Long-Short Flow-Map Perspective for Drifting Models" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Equation 15</span></a> with the mollified kernel <math id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k_{t}^{\epsilon}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k_{t}^{\epsilon}</annotation></semantics></math> in <a href="#S3.E11" title="Equation 11 ‣ 3.1 First-Order Approximation ‣ 3 Long-Short Flow-Map Perspective ‣ A Long-Short Flow-Map Perspective for Drifting Models" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Equation 11</span></a>, their divergences can be also computed in closed form as</span></p>
<table id="S4.E25" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="S4.E25X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E25X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\nabla\cdot u^{*}_{t}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>∇</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\nabla\cdot u^{*}_{t}(x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E25X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{1-t}[\frac{2t}{2(1-t)^{2}+\epsilon}(\frac{\mathbb{E}_{x_{1}\sim p_{1}}[\|x_{1}\|^{2}k^{\epsilon}_{t}(x_{1},x)]}{\mathbb{E}_{x_{1}\sim p_{1}}[k^{\epsilon}_{t}(x_{1},x)]}-\|\frac{\mathbb{E}_{x_{1}\sim p_{1}}[x_{1}k^{\epsilon}_{t}(x_{1},x)]}{\mathbb{E}_{x_{1}\sim p_{1}}[k^{\epsilon}_{t}(x_{1},x)]}\|^{2})-d]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{1-t}[\frac{2t}{2(1-t)^{2}+\epsilon}(\frac{\mathbb{E}_{x_{1}\sim p_{1}}[\|x_{1}\|^{2}k^{\epsilon}_{t}(x_{1},x)]}{\mathbb{E}_{x_{1}\sim p_{1}}[k^{\epsilon}_{t}(x_{1},x)]}-\|\frac{\mathbb{E}_{x_{1}\sim p_{1}}[x_{1}k^{\epsilon}_{t}(x_{1},x)]}{\mathbb{E}_{x_{1}\sim p_{1}}[k^{\epsilon}_{t}(x_{1},x)]}\|^{2})-d]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="2" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(25)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S4.E25Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E25Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\nabla\cdot u^{*}_{1^{-}}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo>∇</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mi>u</mi><msup><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo></msup><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\nabla\cdot u^{*}_{1^{-}}(x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E25Xa.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\frac{1}{1-t}[d-\frac{2t^{2}}{2(1-t)^{2}+\epsilon}(\frac{\mathbb{E}_{x_{t}\sim p_{t}}[\|x_{t}\|^{2}k^{\epsilon}_{t}(x,x_{t})]}{\mathbb{E}_{x_{t}\sim p_{t}}[k^{\epsilon}_{t}(x,x_{t})]}-\|\frac{\mathbb{E}_{x_{t}\sim p_{t}}[x_{t}k^{\epsilon}_{t}(x,x_{t})]}{\mathbb{E}_{x_{t}\sim p_{t}}[k^{\epsilon}_{t}(x,x_{t})]}\|^{2})]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi><mi>ϵ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo stretchy="false">‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\frac{1}{1-t}[d-\frac{2t^{2}}{2(1-t)^{2}+\epsilon}(\frac{\mathbb{E}_{x_{t}\sim p_{t}}[\|x_{t}\|^{2}k^{\epsilon}_{t}(x,x_{t})]}{\mathbb{E}_{x_{t}\sim p_{t}}[k^{\epsilon}_{t}(x,x_{t})]}-\|\frac{\mathbb{E}_{x_{t}\sim p_{t}}[x_{t}k^{\epsilon}_{t}(x,x_{t})]}{\mathbb{E}_{x_{t}\sim p_{t}}[k^{\epsilon}_{t}(x,x_{t})]}\|^{2})]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.Thmtheorem1.p1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">See <a href="#A1.SS4" title="A.4 Proof of ‣ Appendix A Missing Proofs and Theorems ‣ A Long-Short Flow-Map Perspective for Drifting Models" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">subsection A.4</span></a> for the proof.</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S4.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS2.p2.2" class="ltx_p">Therefore, <math id="S4.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G^{\theta}_{0\to 1}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>G</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G^{\theta}_{0\to 1}(x)</annotation></semantics></math> can be calculated as</p>
<table id="S4.E26" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="S4.E26X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E26X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle G^{\theta}_{0\to 1}(x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>G</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle G^{\theta}_{0\to 1}(x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E26X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=G^{\theta}_{0\to 1-\Delta t}(x)-\frac{\Delta t}{2}(\nabla\log p_{1-\Delta t}^{\theta}(x)\cdot u_{1-\Delta t}(x)+\nabla\log p^{\theta}_{1}(x)\cdot u_{1^{-}}(x)+\nabla\cdot u_{1^{-}}(x)+\nabla\cdot u_{1-\Delta t}(x))" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>G</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>log</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>log</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>θ</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><msup><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>∇</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><msup><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo></msup></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>∇</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=G^{\theta}_{0\to 1-\Delta t}(x)-\frac{\Delta t}{2}(\nabla\log p_{1-\Delta t}^{\theta}(x)\cdot u_{1-\Delta t}(x)+\nabla\log p^{\theta}_{1}(x)\cdot u_{1^{-}}(x)+\nabla\cdot u_{1^{-}}(x)+\nabla\cdot u_{1-\Delta t}(x))</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="5" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(26)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S4.E26Xa" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E26Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=G^{\theta}_{0\to 1-\Delta t}(x)-\frac{1}{2}(\nabla\log p^{\theta}_{1-\Delta t}(x)\frac{\mathbb{E}_{x_{1}\sim p_{1}}[(x_{1}-x)k_{1-\Delta t}^{\epsilon}(x_{1},x)]}{\mathbb{E}_{x_{1}\sim p_{1}}[k_{1-\Delta t}^{\epsilon}(x_{1},x)]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>G</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>log</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>k</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mi>ϵ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>k</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mi>ϵ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em">CLOSE</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=G^{\theta}_{0\to 1-\Delta t}(x)-\frac{1}{2}(\nabla\log p^{\theta}_{1-\Delta t}(x)\frac{\mathbb{E}_{x_{1}\sim p_{1}}[(x_{1}-x)k_{1-\Delta t}^{\epsilon}(x_{1},x)]}{\mathbb{E}_{x_{1}\sim p_{1}}[k_{1-\Delta t}^{\epsilon}(x_{1},x)]}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr>
<tr id="S4.E26Xb" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.E26Xb.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle+\nabla\log p^{\theta}_{1}(x)\cdot\frac{\mathbb{E}_{x_{1-\Delta t}\sim p_{1-\Delta t}}[(x-x_{1-\Delta t})k_{1-\Delta t}^{\epsilon}(x,x_{1-\Delta t})]}{\mathbb{E}_{x_{1-\Delta t}\sim p_{1-\Delta t}}[k_{1-\Delta t}^{\epsilon}(x,x_{1-\Delta t})]})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>+</mo><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>log</mi><mi>p</mi><msup><mrow></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msup><msub><mrow></mrow><mn>1</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>k</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mi>ϵ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>k</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mi>ϵ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle+\nabla\log p^{\theta}_{1}(x)\cdot\frac{\mathbb{E}_{x_{1-\Delta t}\sim p_{1-\Delta t}}[(x-x_{1-\Delta t})k_{1-\Delta t}^{\epsilon}(x,x_{1-\Delta t})]}{\mathbb{E}_{x_{1-\Delta t}\sim p_{1-\Delta t}}[k_{1-\Delta t}^{\epsilon}(x,x_{1-\Delta t})]})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
