<p id="A1.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p2.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p2.5.1" class="ltx_text">For <math id="A1.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{1}^{z,*}(z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">∗</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{1}^{z,*}(z)</annotation></semantics></math>, when there exists an auxiliary random variable <math id="A1.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X^{\prime}_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X^{\prime}_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A1.SS5.SSS0.Px1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi_{j}(X^{\prime}_{t})=Z_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>X</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>Z</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi_{j}(X^{\prime}_{t})=Z_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> almost surely, we have</span></p>
<table id="A1.E61" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A1.E61X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.E61X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle u_{1}^{z,*}(z)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>u</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>z</mi><mo rspace="0em">,</mo><mo lspace="0em">∗</mo></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>z</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle u_{1}^{z,*}(z)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
