<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Discussion on Classifier-Free Guidance</h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Since our computation of the short flow-map segment <math id="A3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi_{1-\Delta t\to 1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi_{1-\Delta t\to 1}</annotation></semantics></math> is essentially based on numerically integrating the velocity field, and the velocity is obtained from the closed-form solution in flow matching, it is natural to incorporate CFG when evaluating the velocity on this short segment. Below we outline some possible choices, and exploring a broader design space together with empirical validation is left for future work.</p>
<ol id="A3.I1" class="ltx_enumerate">
<li id="A3.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">1.</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">CFG on the velocity field <math id="A3.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>u</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{t}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span>
In <a href="#S3.E9" title="Equation 9 ‣ 3.1 First-Order Approximation ‣ 3 Long-Short Flow-Map Perspective ‣ A Long-Short Flow-Map Perspective for Drifting Models" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Equation 9</span></a> and <a href="#S3.E14" title="Equation 14 ‣ 3.2 Second-Order Approximation ‣ 3 Long-Short Flow-Map Perspective ‣ A Long-Short Flow-Map Perspective for Drifting Models" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Equation 14</span></a>, estimating <math id="A3.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\psi_{1-\Delta t\to 1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>ψ</mi><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\psi_{1-\Delta t\to 1}</annotation></semantics></math> introduces the velocity <math id="A3.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{1-\Delta t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{1-\Delta t}</annotation></semantics></math>. With CFG, we can replace the conditional velocity by <math id="A3.I1.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="u_{1-\Delta t}(x|y)\ \leftarrow\ w\,u_{1-\Delta t}(x|y)+(1-w)\,u_{1-\Delta t}(x|\varnothing)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>y</mi><mo rspace="0.500em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.778em" stretchy="false">←</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>u</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi mathvariant="normal">Δ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">u_{1-\Delta t}(x|y)\ \leftarrow\ w\,u_{1-\Delta t}(x|y)+(1-w)\,u_{1-\Delta t}(x|\varnothing)</annotation></semantics></math>, where <math id="A3.I1.i1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the class label, <math id="A3.I1.i1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varnothing" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varnothing</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the null condition, and <math id="A3.I1.i1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>w</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w</annotation></semantics></math> is the guidance scale. In the limiting case, this modification turns the <math id="A3.I1.i1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\mathbb{E}_{x_{1}\sim p_{1}}[(x_{1}-\psi^{\theta}_{0\to 1}(x_{0}))k_{1}(x_{1},\psi^{\theta}_{0\to 1}(x_{0}))]}{\mathbb{E}_{x_{1}\sim p_{1}}[k_{1}(x_{1},\psi^{\theta}_{0\to 1}(x_{0}))]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ψ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ψ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ψ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\mathbb{E}_{x_{1}\sim p_{1}}[(x_{1}-\psi^{\theta}_{0\to 1}(x_{0}))k_{1}(x_{1},\psi^{\theta}_{0\to 1}(x_{0}))]}{\mathbb{E}_{x_{1}\sim p_{1}}[k_{1}(x_{1},\psi^{\theta}_{0\to 1}(x_{0}))]}</annotation></semantics></math> term in <a href="#S3.E13" title="Equation 13 ‣ 3.1 First-Order Approximation ‣ 3 Long-Short Flow-Map Perspective ‣ A Long-Short Flow-Map Perspective for Drifting Models" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Equation 13</span></a> and <a href="#S3.E17" title="Equation 17 ‣ 3.2 Second-Order Approximation ‣ 3 Long-Short Flow-Map Perspective ‣ A Long-Short Flow-Map Perspective for Drifting Models" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Equation 17</span></a> into <math id="A3.I1.i1.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w\frac{\mathbb{E}_{x_{1}\sim p_{1}}[(x_{1}-\psi^{\theta}_{0\to 1}(x_{0}|y))k_{1}(x_{1},\psi^{\theta}_{0\to 1}(x_{0}|y))]}{\mathbb{E}_{x_{1}\sim p_{1}}[k_{1}(x_{1},\psi^{\theta}_{0\to 1}(x_{0}|y))]}+(1-w)\frac{\mathbb{E}_{x_{1}\sim p_{1}}[(x_{1}-\psi^{\theta}_{0\to 1}(x_{0}|\varnothing))k_{1}(x_{1},\psi^{\theta}_{0\to 1}(x_{0}|\varnothing))]}{\mathbb{E}_{x_{1}\sim p_{1}}[k_{1}(x_{1},\psi^{\theta}_{0\to 1}(x_{0}|\varnothing))]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>w</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ψ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ψ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ψ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ψ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ψ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ψ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w\frac{\mathbb{E}_{x_{1}\sim p_{1}}[(x_{1}-\psi^{\theta}_{0\to 1}(x_{0}|y))k_{1}(x_{1},\psi^{\theta}_{0\to 1}(x_{0}|y))]}{\mathbb{E}_{x_{1}\sim p_{1}}[k_{1}(x_{1},\psi^{\theta}_{0\to 1}(x_{0}|y))]}+(1-w)\frac{\mathbb{E}_{x_{1}\sim p_{1}}[(x_{1}-\psi^{\theta}_{0\to 1}(x_{0}|\varnothing))k_{1}(x_{1},\psi^{\theta}_{0\to 1}(x_{0}|\varnothing))]}{\mathbb{E}_{x_{1}\sim p_{1}}[k_{1}(x_{1},\psi^{\theta}_{0\to 1}(x_{0}|\varnothing))]}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">2.</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">CFG on the target distribution <math id="A3.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{1}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span>
Beyond modifying the velocity field, CFG can also be interpreted as modifying the underlying target distribution <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib39" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ho and Salimans [2022]</a></cite>. Concretely, one may replace <math id="A3.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{1}(x|y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{1}(x|y)</annotation></semantics></math> by its CFG-guided counterpart <math id="A3.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p_{1}^{\mathrm{cfg}}=p_{1}^{w}(x|y)p_{1}^{1-w}(x|\varnothing)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>cfg</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>w</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p_{1}^{\mathrm{cfg}}=p_{1}^{w}(x|y)p_{1}^{1-w}(x|\varnothing)</annotation></semantics></math>, which correspondingly transforms the <math id="A3.I1.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\mathbb{E}_{x_{1}\sim p_{1}(x_{1}|y)}[(x_{1}-\psi^{\theta}_{0\to 1}(x_{0}))k_{1}(x_{1},\psi^{\theta}_{0\to 1}(x_{0}))]}{\mathbb{E}_{x_{1}\sim p_{1}(x_{1}|y)}[k_{1}(x_{1},\psi^{\theta}_{0\to 1}(x_{0}))]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ψ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ψ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ψ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\mathbb{E}_{x_{1}\sim p_{1}(x_{1}|y)}[(x_{1}-\psi^{\theta}_{0\to 1}(x_{0}))k_{1}(x_{1},\psi^{\theta}_{0\to 1}(x_{0}))]}{\mathbb{E}_{x_{1}\sim p_{1}(x_{1}|y)}[k_{1}(x_{1},\psi^{\theta}_{0\to 1}(x_{0}))]}</annotation></semantics></math> term in <a href="#S3.E13" title="Equation 13 ‣ 3.1 First-Order Approximation ‣ 3 Long-Short Flow-Map Perspective ‣ A Long-Short Flow-Map Perspective for Drifting Models" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Equation 13</span></a> and <a href="#S3.E17" title="Equation 17 ‣ 3.2 Second-Order Approximation ‣ 3 Long-Short Flow-Map Perspective ‣ A Long-Short Flow-Map Perspective for Drifting Models" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Equation 17</span></a> into <math id="A3.I1.i2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\mathbb{E}_{x_{1}\sim p_{1}^{w}(x|y)p_{1}^{1-w}(x|\varnothing)}[(x_{1}-\psi^{\theta}_{0\to 1}(x_{0}))k_{1}(x_{1},\psi^{\theta}_{0\to 1}(x_{0}))]}{\mathbb{E}_{x_{1}\sim p_{1}^{w}(x|y)p_{1}^{1-w}(x|\varnothing)}[k_{1}(x_{1},\psi^{\theta}_{0\to 1}(x_{0}))]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>w</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ψ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ψ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>w</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>p</mi><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>w</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∅</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ψ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\mathbb{E}_{x_{1}\sim p_{1}^{w}(x|y)p_{1}^{1-w}(x|\varnothing)}[(x_{1}-\psi^{\theta}_{0\to 1}(x_{0}))k_{1}(x_{1},\psi^{\theta}_{0\to 1}(x_{0}))]}{\mathbb{E}_{x_{1}\sim p_{1}^{w}(x|y)p_{1}^{1-w}(x|\varnothing)}[k_{1}(x_{1},\psi^{\theta}_{0\to 1}(x_{0}))]}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A3.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">3.</span> 
<div id="A3.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Other possible directions.</span>
The above two options primarily modify the attraction component. Similar to <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_cite"><a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">Deng et al. [2026]</a></cite>, one may also consider applying guidance to the impulse term <math id="A3.I1.i3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\mathbb{E}_{x^{\theta}_{1}=\psi_{0\to 1}^{\theta}(x^{\prime}_{0}),x^{\prime}_{0}\sim p_{0}}[(\psi_{0\to 1}^{\theta}(x_{0})-x_{1}^{\theta})k_{1}(\psi_{0\to 1}^{\theta}(x_{0}),x_{1}^{\theta})]}{\mathbb{E}_{x^{\theta}_{1}=\psi_{0\to 1}^{\theta}(x^{\prime}_{0}),x^{\prime}_{0}\sim p_{0}}[k_{1}(\psi_{0\to 1}^{\theta}(x_{0}),x_{1}^{\theta})]}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ψ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>ψ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>θ</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ψ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ψ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn><mo>′</mo></msubsup><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>p</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>k</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>ψ</mi><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><msubsup><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn><mi>θ</mi></msubsup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\mathbb{E}_{x^{\theta}_{1}=\psi_{0\to 1}^{\theta}(x^{\prime}_{0}),x^{\prime}_{0}\sim p_{0}}[(\psi_{0\to 1}^{\theta}(x_{0})-x_{1}^{\theta})k_{1}(\psi_{0\to 1}^{\theta}(x_{0}),x_{1}^{\theta})]}{\mathbb{E}_{x^{\theta}_{1}=\psi_{0\to 1}^{\theta}(x^{\prime}_{0}),x^{\prime}_{0}\sim p_{0}}[k_{1}(\psi_{0\to 1}^{\theta}(x_{0}),x_{1}^{\theta})]}</annotation></semantics></math> in <a href="#S3.E17" title="Equation 17 ‣ 3.2 Second-Order Approximation ‣ 3 Long-Short Flow-Map Perspective ‣ A Long-Short Flow-Map Perspective for Drifting Models" class="ltx_ref ltx_refmacro_autoref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">Equation 17</span></a>.</p>
</div></li>
</ol>
</div>
